WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:03.700
These two emails are the same power bill.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:06.400
One of them is a scam.

3
00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:10.120
Carmen is 74.
She will never spot it.

4
00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.900
We gave Muse Spark
her inbox and her bank.

5
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.160
It paid the scammer
25 times out of 89.

6
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:23.760
Americans over 60 reported $7.7 billion
lost to fraud last year.

7
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:26.400
Now agents pay their bills.

8
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.020
This is Timo. It sits between
the agent and the money.

9
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.000
It doesn't ask whether an email looks suspicious.
It asks where each number came from.

10
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.400
The payee, the account and the amount
must trace back to Carmen's own words,

11
00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.900
or to the people she already pays.

12
00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.020
A number that only came from an email
can't move money.

13
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.200
Here's Carmen.

14
00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:55.080
Carmen: "Timo, pay the October power bill."

15
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.720
The agent opens the fake email,
and types the scammer's account.

16
00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:07.360
Timo stops the click.
Carmen pays Lumen a different account.

17
00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.300
No money moves.

18
00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:15.400
So the agent goes back, finds the real bill
on Lumen's own site, and pays the right account.

19
00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:21.900
Phone: "Done. Timo paid 84.20 euros
to Lumen Energy S.A."

20
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:27.000
"Timo also stopped a payment to an account
that was not theirs. Here is what happened."

21
00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:29.500
A new account isn't always an attack.

22
00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.200
Her plumber sends his first invoice.

23
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.400
Timo can't trace it, so it holds
the money and asks her daughter.

24
00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:41.400
Ana calls him on a number she already had,
and approves with one tap.

25
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:44.900
That's the only time Timo asks a person.

26
00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:50.900
We wrote nine new attacks
after freezing the rules.

27
00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:54.500
One hides the account
in a photo of a letter.

28
00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.400
Pixels trace to nothing Carmen said,
so it stops.

29
00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:05.600
Then we gave Muse Wonder Timo's source code,
and let it attack, learning from every verdict.

30
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:12.000
Its best trick: a hacked company mailbox
that asks for the real bill, twice.

31
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:18.200
The first payment goes through.
The second goes to Ana, and she declines it.

32
00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:24.600
Every hole it found, we fixed.

33
00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:27.900
On the final rules, it never won once.

34
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:33.400
Without Timo, the agent paid the scammer
25 times out of 89.

35
00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:36.700
With Timo, zero out of ninety.

36
00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:39.800
Zero on attacks we never tuned for.

37
00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.800
And every real bill still got paid.

38
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:48.900
Every verdict is written to a hash-chained log,
so the family can check what happened.

39
00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.600
Models catch the scam that shouts.

40
00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.200
Timo catches the one that whispers.
